<h2>Parts of a Homeowners Claim People Often Forget</h2>
<h3>Other structures</h3>
<p>Detached garages, sheds, fences and carports are usually covered under a separate part of the policy with its own limit. Fences and outbuildings are frequently damaged in Gulf Coast storms and frequently left off the first estimate.</p>
<h3>Personal property</h3>
<p>Furniture, clothing, appliances and electronics damaged by a covered peril belong in the claim. A photo inventory, even one built after the fact from phone pictures, is far better than a rough guess.</p>
<h3>Additional living expense</h3>
<p>If the home cannot be lived in during repairs, many policies pay reasonable extra costs such as lodging and increased meal expenses. Keep every receipt.</p>
<h3>Debris removal and emergency repairs</h3>
<p>Tarping, board-up, water extraction and tree removal from the structure may be reimbursable. Photograph conditions before and after mitigation work.</p>

